  "notes": "Warm off-white canvas with deep teal sidebar and teal selection outline; red reserved for the leave/no-date conditions, amber for 'can't be swapped'. Blocked calendar days use a diagonal hatched gradient with the blocking reason printed inside each cell (and in aria-label), workable days get a teal outline and 'N open'. Exception switches appear twice (in alert's 'Closest paths' and in the picker's Exceptions box) and stay synced; enabling one re-computes workable days and shows the legal-requirement note (34 CFR 300.321(e)). Queue groups have colored dots (red/amber/teal) as triage categories. Constraint chips on cards (After 12:30 PM, SLP Tue/Thu, Somali). Two panes scroll independently."
